        "passage": "Mark the letter A, B, C or D on your answer sheet to indicate the best arrangement of utterances or \nsentences to make a meaningful exchange or text in each of the following questions \nQuestion 23. \nSubject: Invitation to Interview for Marketing Associate Position \nDear Jane Smith, \na. The interview will take place on Thursday, February 1st, at 10:30 AM via Zoom. \nb. We are excited to invite you to an interview for the Marketing Associate position at BrightSpark \nSolutions. \nc. We look forward to learning more about you and sharing details about our team and the role. \nd. The interview will last approximately 45 minutes and will include a discussion about your experience \nand skills. \ne. Please confirm your availability by replying to this email, and let us know if you require any assistance \naccessing the platform. \nBest regards, \nMichael Davis \nHR Manager \nBrightSpark Solutions \nA. e – d – a – c – b \nB. b – a – e – d – c \nC. c – a – e – b – d \nD. d – e – c – a – b \nQuestion 24. \na. With its high adaptability to different climates, maize continues to play a significant role in global \nagriculture and economies. \nb. Beyond its culinary uses, maize is also an important source of animal feed and biofuel. \nc. Maize, also known as corn, is one of the most widely grown cereal crops in the world \nd. Maize is incredibly versatile and is used in a variety of forms, such as cornmeal, popcorn, and corn \nsyrup, making it an essential ingredient in numerous food products \ne. Originating in Mesoamerica, it has become a staple food in many countries, particularly in North and \nSouth America. \nA. e-d-c-a-b \nB. c-e-b-d-a \nC. b-e-d-a-c \nD. c- e-d-b-a \n\nQuestion 25. \na. It consists of strings, usually made of steel or nylon, which are strummed or plucked to produce sound. \nb. Guitars have been central to many music genres, from rock and jazz to classical and folk, allowing \nmusicians to express themselves creatively. A guitar shares some physical similarities to some other \ninstruments. \nc. Learning to play the guitar can be both challenging and rewarding, requiring practice and technique to \nmaster chords, scales, and melodies. \nd. Whether played solo or as part of a band, the guitar remains an iconic instrument in modern music, \ncaptivating audiences worldwide. \ne. It comes in various forms, including acoustic, electric, and classical, each offering unique sounds and \nplaying experiences. \nf. The guitar is one of the most popular and versatile musical instruments in the world. \nA. a-b-d-c-f-e \nB. f-e-b-a-c-d \nC. f-e-d-c-b-a \nD. e-a-b-d-c-f \nQuestion 26. \na. They are giving out leaflets. \nb. The scene shows a young man and a boy at the entrance to the museum. \nc. And most of the passers-by neither look at the boy nor take a leaflet. \nd. They do not look very happy. They are tired and disappointed. \ne. The boy does not even look at any passers-by when he gives him a leaflet. \nf. I have a chance to look at one of the scenes of the film. \nA. b-a-c-e-d-f \nB. b-e-c-d-a-f \nC. f-b-a-d-e-c \nD. f-b-a-c-e-d",
